    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="f_renal_function" name="renal function" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <blockquote>
              <p>1.0: increased kidney function
1.0: normal kidney function (healthy control)
&lt;1.0: decreased kidney function</p>
            </blockquote>
            <p>Renal function relative to the healthy glomerular filtration rate
GFR_base of 101 ml/min; a measured creatinine clearance of X ml/min
is the renal function X/101 (<code>pkpdsim.impairment.RENAL_FUNCTION_GFR</code>).</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="GFR_base" name="glomerular filtration rate (healthy)" value="101" units="ml_per_min" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The GFR of healthy kidneys, independent of the body weight; the GFR
is <code>f_renal_function</code> times this rate.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="fu_api" name="fraction unbound in plasma apixaban" value="0.131" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="APIEX_f" name="renal clearance of unbound apixaban relative to the GFR" value="1.01497104264872" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The renal clearance of apixaban is APIEX_f times the filtration of
its unbound fraction, fu_api * GFR: 1 is filtration alone, above 1 a
net secretion, below 1 a net reabsorption. Renal clearance 0.93 l/h
(Frost2021): 0.93 l/h / (0.131 * 6.06 l/h) = 1.17.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
        <distrib:listOfUncertainties>
          <distrib:uncertainty distrib:name="fit PK_20261017_103232__85dfa">
